# 36. Dependency Patching

Modern applications depend on third-party libraries.

Example:

```text
Application
├── Framework
├── Database driver
├── Logging library
├── Authentication library
└── JavaScript packages
```

A vulnerability in one dependency can affect the application.

Therefore:

> **Patch management must include application dependencies, not only operating systems.**

---

# 37. Firmware Patching

Patching is not limited to applications and operating systems.

It may also involve:

- Routers
- Switches
- Firewalls
- BIOS/UEFI
- Storage systems
- IoT devices
- Security appliances

Firmware updates should be carefully tested because failure can affect device availability.

---

# 38. Cloud Patch Management

Cloud environments introduce additional considerations.

Depending on the service model:

### IaaS

The organization may be responsible for patching the operating system and applications.

### PaaS

The cloud provider may manage more of the underlying platform.

### SaaS

The provider generally manages the underlying application infrastructure.

### Important

> **Patch responsibility depends on the cloud service model and shared-responsibility arrangement.**

