# 40. Common Patch Management Mistakes

## Mistake 1: Patching without inventory

You may miss systems.

## Mistake 2: Installing everything blindly

Updates can cause compatibility issues.

## Mistake 3: No testing

Production problems may occur.

## Mistake 4: No rollback/recovery plan

Recovery becomes difficult.

## Mistake 5: No verification

You don't know whether remediation worked.

## Mistake 6: Ignoring applications

Only patching the OS is insufficient.

## Mistake 7: Ignoring firmware

Network/security devices can also have vulnerabilities.

## Mistake 8: Ignoring EOL software

Unsupported software can remain vulnerable.

## Mistake 9: Using only CVSS for priority

Business risk and exposure also matter.

## Mistake 10: No documentation

You cannot easily demonstrate compliance or track exceptions.

